# React Native UI Package

## Structure

- `hooks/` — socket lifecycle + Zustand stores
- `ui/` — presentational screens/components
- `socket.ts` — keyed Socket.IO factories (recreate when user/room/url changes)
- `types/` — shared client event payloads
- Re-export public API from `src/index.ts`

## Patterns

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — stable callback refs; reconcile optimistic IDs
callbacksRef.current.onMessageReceived?.(data);
reconcileMessage(clientMessageId, serverMessage);

// ❌ BAD — put inline consumer callbacks in effect deps (listener churn)
useEffect(() => { ... }, [onMessageReceived]);
```

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — media cleanup via refs so unmount/remote-end always stops tracks
localStreamRef.current?.getTracks().forEach((track) => track.stop());

// ❌ BAD — cleanup closes over a stale null localStream state
```

- Prefer peer-ready / join acknowledgements over hard-coded `setTimeout` races
- Keep peerDependencies for RN, WebRTC, InCallManager, socket.io-client, zustand
- Match existing double-quote / TypeScript style in this package
